##  Dashboards

The project includes five interactive dashboards developed to analyze different aspects of employee data and understand the factors associated with employee attrition.

### 1. Age and Gender Distribution

This dashboard focuses on the demographic characteristics of employees. It analyzes the distribution of employees based on age and gender and helps provide an overview of the workforce composition.

### 2. Employee Attrition Analysis

This dashboard focuses on employee attrition and identifies patterns related to employees who stayed with the organization and those who left. It provides an overall view of attrition and helps analyze how attrition varies across different employee categories.

### 3. Job Satisfaction and Environment

This dashboard analyzes employee job satisfaction and workplace-related factors. It helps understand employee satisfaction levels and their relationship with different workplace and job-related attributes.

### 4. Lifestyle and Travel

This dashboard focuses on lifestyle and work-related factors such as business travel and other employee lifestyle characteristics. It helps analyze how these factors may be associated with employee attrition.

### 5. Salary and Compensation

This dashboard analyzes employee salary and compensation-related factors. It provides insights into employee income and compensation patterns and helps examine their relationship with employee attrition.
